  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123905,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary\nACCIDENTAL RELEASE PREVENTION AND ACTION POLICIES\nThe accidental release prevention and action policies for the Natrium NGL Extraction and Fractionation Plant are maintained in the facility's Emergency Action Plan and RMP Manual. Williams Partners Operating LLC is committed to the safety and health of its employees, contractors and visitors. This commitment is demonstrated in the design, installation, operation and maintenance programs developed and implemented specifically for this\nfacility. Operation and maintenance personnel are trained in the appropriate emergency action procedures to follow in the event of an accidental release. However, accident prevention is the ultimate goal and as such a site-specific mechanical integrity program is being implemented and maintained.\n\nFACILITY DESCRIPTION AND REGULATED SUNSTANCES\nThe Natrium Extraction and Fractionation Processing Plant (SIC Code: 1321) is a natural gas processing plant with natural gas liquids (NGL) processing capability (utilizing four (4) permitted cryogenic plants and 2 fractionation trains) located approximately four (4) miles northwest of Proctor, Marshall County, WV along the east bank of the Ohio River. The facility has the capability to both process large amounts of raw natural gas (by separating out the liquids, drying it, and removing impurities) and to fractionate NGLs into usable components. NGLs are generally defined to be the lighter liquid components entrained in the gas stream as opposed to \u0093condensate\u0094 which is the heavier, pentane plus (C5+) fraction of higher boiling point components that are separated at the well-head under standard conditions. NGLs - both after separation from gas pipelined to the site, as well as NGLs sent to the site via pipeline, truck, railcar, or barge - are separated (or \u0093fractionated\u0094) into their constituent organic compounds. The compounds ethane, propane, n-butane, i-butane, and natural gasoline are produced by the fractionation process.\n\nGENE"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123905,
      "SummaryText": "RAL ACCIDENTAL RELEASE PREVENTION PROGRAM\nThe Natrium NGL Extraction and Fractionation Plant has developed and implemented a site-specific accidental release prevention program that consists of a detailed facility mechanical integrity program and employee training program. The mechanical integrity program was developed under the guidelines of manufacturer written recommendations, recognized/generally accepted good engineering practices, industry/regulatory standards\nand past operation history. Employee training was designed to ensure/document employee understanding of facility operation and maintenance requirements.\n\nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY\nThe Natrium NGL Extraction and Fractionation Plant has had no accidental releases in the past 5 years that have resulted in offsite consequences.\n\nEMERGENCY ACTION PROGRAM\nThe Natrium NGL Extraction and Fractionation Plant has developed and maintains a site-specific Emergency Action Plan (EAP) that includes actions to take in the event of an uncontrolled release of a hazardous substance. The EAP includes the names and phone numbers not only of company personnel but also the names and phone numbers of\nsupport services (contractor, police departments, fire departments, medical services/hospitals, regulatory agencies, LEPC, etc.) that may be called upon for assistance. Liaison with these agencies is maintained to ensure timely and proper responses. Employee understanding of their responsibilities during an emergency situation is high priority.\n\nPLANNED CHANGES TO IMPROVE SAFETY\nWilliams Partners Operating LLC believes safety is an issue that can always be improved upon. Williams continues to look for, develop, and implement programs that will improve an employee's ability to identify and correct potential workplace hazards. Williams also endeavors to ensure policies, programs and procedures are developed and implemented to meet applicable laws, rules and regulations. Employee understanding of these policies, programs and procedur"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 2,
      "FacilityID": 1000123905,
      "SummaryText": "es is high priority. Currently, the facility is planning to close the recommendations from the August 2025 Process Hazard Analysis. Those changes are intended, and planned, to improve safety at the facility."
    }
  ]
